*Statement 13:** If the cat sees the squirrel, it must be kind. \n     - This requires the cat to be kind. Since there\u2019s no rule preventing an entity from being both rough and kind, and no contradiction in the premises, this is acceptable. Thus, the cat is now also kind.\n   - **Statement 21:** The rabbit eats the mouse (fact 9), so the rabbit must be rough. This aligns with **Statement 18**, which requires the rabbit (now rough) to see the cat (fact 10), consistent with existing data.\n   - **Statement 20:** No entity is confirmed to both visit the rabbit and see the squirrel, so this rule doesn\u2019t affect the conclusion.\n\n**Final Conclusion:**\nThe cat seeing the squirrel is **true** based on the derived rules. The only potential issue (the cat needing to be kind) is resolved without contradiction.\n\n**Answer:**  \nA) True",
